The Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog
-------------------------------------------------

src/kev_catalog/schema/kev_catalog.yaml, src/kev_catalog/datamodel/, project/
and the examples under tests/data/ model the JSON format of the Known Exploited
Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog, which the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure
Security Agency (CISA) of the United States publishes at
https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog. CISA's data files
and JSON schema are mirrored at https://github.com/cisagov/kev-data.

CISA's JSON schema states no version. This project names the edition it renders
by the date of the commit that last changed the file in kev-data, 2026-09-17
(commit d98075f22b11), and pins the file by its git object hash and SHA-256.

The KEV data is distributed under Creative Commons Zero 1.0 Universal (CC0 1.0).
The kev-data repository's LICENSE file opens with CISA's own statement of the
position, which this project keeps to: the data may be used in any legal way;
information at a third-party link in the data is bound by that third party's
policies and licences; and use of the information does not authorize use of the
CISA Logo or the DHS Seal, and must not be read as an endorsement by CISA or the
Department of Homeland Security (DHS). This project is not CISA's or DHS's, and
its use implies no endorsement by either.

Under those terms this repository holds exact copies:
tests/upstream/known_exploited_vulnerabilities_schema.json, tests/upstream/LICENSE
(the file above, with the full CC0 1.0 text), and the entries under
tests/data/kev-data/extract/. The free text in those entries, and the addresses
it names, are CISA's. The schema's descriptions are this project's own words.

